<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Turkish translation — full UI coverage. Sen-form (informal 2nd person singular)
throughout. SOV word order where natural. Brand name "ClothesCast" stays verbatim.

What is NOT overridden, by design:
- `app_name` — brand identifier, identical across locales.
- `insight_time_am` / `_pm` / `_midnight` / `_noon` (and the *_minutes
  variants) — English-only spoken-time formatter helpers. Turkish locales
  use `insight_time_hour` / `insight_time_hour_minutes` ("%1$d" / "%1$d:%2$02d")
  which are translated below; the AM/PM keys exist for `Locale.language == "en"`
  paths only and would never be read in a Turkish runtime.

Picker labels under `settings_region_language_*` and
`settings_tts_voice_locale_*` give the Turkish names for every offered locale.
The locale tag stored on disk (en-US / fr-CA / zh-CN) is unchanged; only the
displayed label localizes.
-->
